Notebook[{
Cell["Graphical calculus \:00a72.3\:20132.7: double duals, isotopy, traces and sphericity", "Title"],
Cell["Turaev & Virelizier, Monoidal Categories and Topological Field Theory, pp. 38\:201350 \:00b7 sections 40\:201348 \:00b7 continues graphical-calculus-2.1-simplify.nb, pivotal-2.1.3.wl and penrose-2.2.wl", "Subtitle"],
Cell["By Dara O Shayda and Noor Hoshino (\:661f\:91ce\:30cc\:30fc\:30eb)", "Text"],
Cell["39. Setup", "Section"],
Cell["The first cell loads the engine from this folder (Desktop/Research/Monoidal Graphical Calculus); the second loads the code of this notebook, which is also saved on its own as pivotal-2.3-2.7.wl. The GraphicalCalculusKernel loads the same package.", "Text"],
Cell["ClearAll[\"Global`*\"];\n(* the engine: sections 0\:201319 (\:00a72.1.1\:20132.1.2), 20\:201327 (\:00a72.1.3), 30\:201335 (\:00a72.2), all in this folder *)\ndir = FileNameJoin[{$HomeDirectory, \"Desktop\", \"Research\", \"Monoidal Graphical Calculus\"}];\n(* With, not Module: the first notebook starts with ClearAll[\"Global`*\"], which would clear the loader's own variables *)\nWith[{cells = Cases[Get[FileNameJoin[{dir, \"graphical-calculus-2.1-simplify.nb\"}]], Cell[c_, \"Input\" | \"Code\", ___] :> c, Infinity]},\n Scan[Quiet@Check[TimeConstrained[ToExpression[#, StandardForm]; Null, 120], Null] &, cells];\n Print[\"Loaded \", Length[cells], \" code cells from graphical-calculus-2.1-simplify.nb\"]];\ndir = FileNameJoin[{$HomeDirectory, \"Desktop\", \"Research\", \"Monoidal Graphical Calculus\"}];\nQuiet[Get[FileNameJoin[{dir, \"pivotal-2.1.3.wl\"}]]]; Quiet[Get[FileNameJoin[{dir, \"penrose-2.2.wl\"}]]];\nPrint[\"Loaded pivotal-2.1.3.wl and penrose-2.2.wl\"];", "Input"],
Cell["40. \:00a72.3.1 The double duals: \:03c8_X and the rules of Lemmas 2.2\:20132.3", "Section"],
Cell["X** = (X* )* is its own object, written \"X**\". An arc coloured X* and pointing up contributes X** to a source or target.\n   \:03c8_X : X \:2192 X** is (\:1ebdv_X \:2297 id_X** )(id_X \:2297 coev_X* ). It is drawn as a box \:03c8_X, and its inverse as a box \:03c8\:207b\:00b9_X.\n   Lemma 2.3 rewrites a cap or cup coloured X* as a cap or cup coloured X with \:03c8^{\:00b11} on the X** leg:\n     ev_X*  = \:1ebdv_X (\:03c8\:207b\:00b9_X \:2297 id_X* ),      \:1ebdv_X*  = ev_X (id_X* \:2297 \:03c8\:207b\:00b9_X),\n     coev_X* = (id_X* \:2297 \:03c8_X) c\:0303oev_X,     c\:0303oev_X* = (\:03c8_X \:2297 id_X* ) coev_X.\n   With \"inverse boxes\" (\:03c8\:207b\:00b9\:03c8 = id, \:03c8\:03c8\:207b\:00b9 = id) these rules decide Lemma 2.2, Lemma 2.3, Lemma 2.4 and Exercise 2.3.3.\n   When an input already identifies X** with X (as the editor does), the strict forms apply: ev_X* = \:1ebdv_X and \:03c8_X = id_X.", "Text"],
Cell["psi[x_] := Subscript[\"\\[Psi]\", x];\npsiInv[x_] := Subscript[Superscript[\"\\[Psi]\", \"-1\"], x];\npsiB[x_] := B[psi[x], {x}, {star[star[x]]}];\npsiInvB[x_] := B[psiInv[x], {star[star[x]]}, {x}];\n\n(* Lemma 2.3, one cap or cup at a time *)\nlemma23[{a_, B[Subscript[\"ev\", c_?starQ], {cc_, c_}, {}]}] /; cc === star[c] :=\n  With[{x = unstar[c]}, {{a, psiInvB[x]}, {a, B[evR[x], {x, c}, {}]}}];\nlemma23[{a_, B[Subscript[OverTilde[\"ev\"], c_?starQ], {c_, cc_}, {}]}] /; cc === star[c] :=\n  With[{x = unstar[c]}, {{a + 1, psiInvB[x]}, {a, B[evL[x], {c, x}, {}]}}];\nlemma23[{a_, B[Subscript[\"coev\", c_?starQ], {}, {c_, cc_}]}] /; cc === star[c] :=\n  With[{x = unstar[c]}, {{a, B[coevR[x], {}, {c, x}]}, {a + 1, psiB[x]}}];\nlemma23[{a_, B[Subscript[OverTilde[\"coev\"], c_?starQ], {}, {cc_, c_}]}] /; cc === star[c] :=\n  With[{x = unstar[c]}, {{a, B[coevL[x], {}, {x, c}]}, {a, psiB[x]}}];\nlemma23[_] := $Failed;\n\n(* the strict forms, X** = X and \:03c8_X = id_X, for inputs written that way *)\nlemma23strict[{a_, B[Subscript[\"ev\", c_?starQ], {x_, c_}, {}]}] /; x === unstar[c] := {{a, B[evR[x], {x, c}, {}]}};\nlemma23strict[{a_, B[Subscript[OverTilde[\"ev\"], c_?starQ], {c_, x_}, {}]}] /; x === unstar[c] := {{a, B[evL[x], {c, x}, {}]}};\nlemma23strict[{a_, B[Subscript[\"coev\", c_?starQ], {}, {c_, x_}]}] /; x === unstar[c] := {{a, B[coevR[x], {}, {c, x}]}};\nlemma23strict[{a_, B[Subscript[OverTilde[\"coev\"], c_?starQ], {}, {x_, c_}]}] /; x === unstar[c] := {{a, B[coevL[x], {}, {x, c}]}};\nlemma23strict[_] := $Failed;\npsiStrict[{_, B[Subscript[\"\\[Psi]\" | Superscript[\"\\[Psi]\", \"-1\"], x_], {x_}, {x_}]}] := {};\npsiStrict[_] := $Failed;\n\n(* caps and cups on \:2297 for inputs with X** = X: the same nests, with the dual of X* written X *)\nflipC[c_String] := If[starQ[c], unstar[c], star[c]];\nflipList[ps_List] := Reverse[flipC /@ ps];\nnestCapsStrict[{a_, B[Subscript[\"ev\", x_String], i_, {}]}] /; Length[partsOf[x]] > 1 :=\n  With[{p = First[partsOf[x]], r = Rest[partsOf[x]]},\n   If[i =!= Join[flipList[r], {flipC[p], p}, r], $Failed,\n    {{a + Length[r], B[Subscript[\"ev\", p], {flipC[p], p}, {}]}, {a, B[Subscript[\"ev\", joinParts[r]], Join[flipList[r], r], {}]}}]];\nnestCapsStrict[{a_, B[Subscript[\"coev\", x_String], {}, o_]}] /; Length[partsOf[x]] > 1 :=\n  With[{p = First[partsOf[x]], r = Rest[partsOf[x]]},\n   If[o =!= Join[{p}, r, flipList[r], {flipC[p]}], $Failed,\n    {{a, B[Subscript[\"coev\", p], {}, {p, flipC[p]}]}, {a + 1, B[Subscript[\"coev\", joinParts[r]], {}, Join[r, flipList[r]]]}}]];\nnestCapsStrict[{a_, B[Subscript[OverTilde[\"ev\"], x_String], i_, {}]}] /; Length[partsOf[x]] > 1 :=\n  With[{p = First[partsOf[x]], r = Rest[partsOf[x]]},\n   If[i =!= Join[{p}, r, flipList[r], {flipC[p]}], $Failed,\n    {{a + 1, B[Subscript[OverTilde[\"ev\"], joinParts[r]], Join[r, flipList[r]], {}]}, {a, B[Subscript[OverTilde[\"ev\"], p], {p, flipC[p]}, {}]}}]];\nnestCapsStrict[{a_, B[Subscript[OverTilde[\"coev\"], x_String], {}, o_]}] /; Length[partsOf[x]] > 1 :=\n  With[{p = First[partsOf[x]], r = Rest[partsOf[x]]},\n   If[o =!= Join[flipList[r], {flipC[p], p}, r], $Failed,\n    {{a, B[Subscript[OverTilde[\"coev\"], joinParts[r]], {}, Join[flipList[r], r]]}, {a + Length[r], B[Subscript[OverTilde[\"coev\"], p], {}, {flipC[p], p}]}}]];\nnestCapsStrict[_] := $Failed;\nnestCapsD[l_] := With[{r = nestCaps[l]}, If[r =!= $Failed, r, nestCapsStrict[l]]];\n\n(* inverse boxes: u\:207b\:00b9 directly above u on the same line, or u above u\:207b\:00b9, cancel *)\ninverses = {};                                   (* declared pairs {u, u\:207b\:00b9} *)\ninvQ[s1_, s2_] := MemberQ[inverses, {s1, s2} | {s2, s1}] ||\n   MatchQ[{s1, s2}, {Subscript[\"\\[Psi]\", x_], Subscript[Superscript[\"\\[Psi]\", \"-1\"], x_]} | {Subscript[Superscript[\"\\[Psi]\", \"-1\"], x_], Subscript[\"\\[Psi]\", x_]}];\ncancelInv[{a_, B[s1_, {c_}, {d_}]}, {a_, B[s2_, {d_}, {c_}]}] /; invQ[s1, s2] := {};\ncancelInv[__] := $Failed;\n\n(* naturality of \:03c8 (\:00a72.5.1): f** \:03c8_X = \:03c8_Y f, for a box f : X \:2192 Y *)\nnatPsi[{a_, B[Subscript[\"\\[Psi]\", x_], {x_}, {xx_}]}, {a_, B[g_String, {xx_}, {yy_}]}] /;\n   StringEndsQ[g, \"**\"] && yy === star[star[unstar[unstar[yy]]]] && StringEndsQ[yy, \"**\"] :=\n  With[{y = StringDrop[yy, -2]}, {{a, B[StringDrop[g, -2], {x}, {y}]}, {a, B[psi[y], {y}, {yy}]}}];\nnatPsi[__] := $Failed;\n\n(* the four constructions of Lemma 2.2, as layered diagrams *)\npsiDef[x_] := LD[{x}, {{1, B[coevL[star[x]], {}, {star[x], star[star[x]]}]}, {0, B[evR[x], {x, star[x]}, {}]}}];      (* \:03c8_X *)\nphiDef[x_] := LD[{x}, {{0, B[coevR[star[x]], {}, {star[star[x]], star[x]}]}, {1, B[evL[x], {star[x], x}, {}]}}];      (* \:03c6_X *)\nthetaDef[x_] := LD[{star[star[x]]}, {{0, B[coevL[x], {}, {x, star[x]}]}, {1, B[evR[star[x]], {star[x], star[star[x]]}, {}]}}];   (* \:03d1_X *)\nnuDef[x_] := LD[{star[star[x]]}, {{1, B[coevR[x], {}, {star[x], x}]}, {0, B[evL[star[x]], {star[star[x]], star[x]}, {}]}}];     (* \:03bd_X *)", "Input"],
Cell["41. \:00a72.3.2 Generalized evaluations ev_S, coev_S and the isomorphisms \:03a8_S", "Section"],
Cell["A tuple S of signed objects {X, \"+\"} or {X, \"-\"} (section 32) has a dual tuple S* = ((X_n, \:2212\:03b5_n), \:2026, (X_1, \:2212\:03b5_1)).\n   ev_S : X_S* \:2297 X_S \:2192 \|01d7d9 is a nest of caps, the innermost on X_1: ev_(X,+) = ev_X and ev_(X,\:2212) = \:1ebdv_X.\n   coev_S : \|01d7d9 \:2192 X_S \:2297 X_S* is a nest of cups: coev_(X,+) = coev_X and coev_(X,\:2212) = c\:0303oev_X.\n   \:03a8_S : X_S \:2192 (X_S* )* is \:03c8_X on every (X,+) entry and id_X* on every (X,\:2212) entry; the target is written strand by strand, which is how the tensor rules of section 30 read (X_S* )*.", "Text"],
Cell["dualTuple[s_List] := Reverse[{#[[1]], If[#[[2]] === \"+\", \"-\", \"+\"]} & /@ s];\ncapOf[{x_, \"+\"}] := B[evL[x], {star[x], x}, {}];\ncapOf[{x_, \"-\"}] := B[evR[x], {x, star[x]}, {}];\ncupOf[{x_, \"+\"}] := B[coevL[x], {}, {x, star[x]}];\ncupOf[{x_, \"-\"}] := B[coevR[x], {}, {star[x], x}];\nevS[s_List] := With[{n = Length[s]}, LD[Join[XS[dualTuple[s]], XS[s]], Table[{n - k, capOf[s[[k]]]}, {k, n}]]];\ncoevS[s_List] := LD[{}, Table[{k - 1, cupOf[s[[k]]]}, {k, Length[s]}]];\nPsiS[s_List] := LD[XS[s], Flatten[MapIndexed[If[#1[[2]] === \"+\", {{#2[[1]] - 1, psiB[#1[[1]]]}}, {}] &, s], 1]];\nPsiInvS[s_List] := LD[Last[rows[PsiS[s]]], Flatten[MapIndexed[If[#1[[2]] === \"+\", {{#2[[1]] - 1, psiInvB[#1[[1]]]}}, {}] &, s], 1]];\n(* the tensor-coloured caps and cups of section 30, on X_S *)\nevXS[s_List] := With[{c = XS[s]}, LD[Join[dualList[c], c], {{0, B[evL[joinParts[c]], Join[dualList[c], c], {}]}}]];\ncoevXS[s_List] := With[{c = XS[s]}, LD[{}, {{0, B[coevL[joinParts[c]], {}, Join[c, dualList[c]]]}}]];\nevRXS[s_List] := With[{c = XS[s]}, LD[Join[c, dualList[c]], {{0, B[evR[joinParts[c]], Join[c, dualList[c]], {}]}}]];\ncoevRXS[s_List] := With[{c = XS[s]}, LD[{}, {{0, B[coevR[joinParts[c]], {}, Join[dualList[c], c]]}}]];", "Input"],
Cell["42. \:00a72.4 Isotopy invariance: the dual of a diagram, and a box turned through 360\:00b0", "Section"],
Cell["dualLD[d] is the left expression of Figure 2.3 wrapped round any diagram d : S \:2192 T: the cup coev_S on the right, d in the middle, the cap ev_T on the left. It represents d* : T* \:2192 S*.\n   Applied twice it turns the diagram through 360\:00b0: Lemma 2.5 and the naturality of \:03c8 (\:00a72.5.1) say that \:03a8_T\:207b\:00b9 d** \:03a8_S = d.", "Text"],
Cell["dualLD[ld_LD] := Module[{s = First[rows[ld]], t = Last[rows[ld]], n},\n   n = Length[t];\n   LD[dualList[t],\n    Join[If[s === {}, {}, {{n, B[If[Length[s] == 1, coevL[First[s]], coevL[joinParts[s]]], {}, Join[s, dualList[s]]]}}],\n     {#[[1]] + n, #[[2]]} & /@ ld[[2]],\n     If[t === {}, {}, {{0, B[If[Length[t] == 1, evL[First[t]], evL[joinParts[t]]], Join[dualList[t], t], {}]}}]]]];\npsiRow[cs_List] := LD[cs, Table[{k - 1, psiB[cs[[k]]]}, {k, Length[cs]}]];\npsiInvRow[cs_List] := LD[star /@ (star /@ cs), Table[{k - 1, psiInvB[cs[[k]]]}, {k, Length[cs]}]];\nrotate360[ld_LD] := stackL[psiRow[First[rows[ld]]], dualLD[dualLD[ld]], psiInvRow[Last[rows[ld]]]];", "Input"],
Cell["43. \:00a72.6 Traces and dimensions", "Section"],
Cell["tr_l(f) = ev_X (id_X* \:2297 f) c\:0303oev_X and tr_r(f) = \:1ebdv_X (f \:2297 id_X* ) coev_X, for f : X \:2192 X given as a layered diagram.\n   dim_l(X) = tr_l(id_X) = ev_X c\:0303oev_X and dim_r(X) = tr_r(id_X) = \:1ebdv_X coev_X.\n   \"trace symmetry\" turns a loop so that the boxes on it start at the earliest one in a fixed order. With the slides of Figure 2.4, which move f* off the other leg, it decides tr(pq) = tr(qp) and the identities of \:00a72.6.1.\n   \"sphericity\" (\:00a72.7.1) is used only for spherical categories: it turns a right loop \:1ebdv_X (f \:2297 id) coev_X into the left loop ev_X (id \:2297 f) c\:0303oev_X.", "Text"],
Cell["loopColour[cs_List] := If[Length[cs] == 1, First[cs], joinParts[cs]];\ntrL[f_LD] := With[{c = First[rows[f]], n = Length[First[rows[f]]]},\n   LD[{}, Join[{{0, B[coevR[loopColour[c]], {}, Join[dualList[c], c]]}}, {#[[1]] + n, #[[2]]} & /@ f[[2]],\n     {{0, B[evL[loopColour[c]], Join[dualList[c], c], {}]}}]]];\ntrR[f_LD] := With[{c = First[rows[f]]},\n   LD[{}, Join[{{0, B[coevL[loopColour[c]], {}, Join[c, dualList[c]]]}}, f[[2]],\n     {{0, B[evR[loopColour[c]], Join[c, dualList[c]], {}]}}]]];\ndimL[x_] := trL[idL[{x}]];\ndimR[x_] := trR[idL[{x}]];\n\n(* a loop: a cup at a, a chain of one-line boxes on one leg, a cap at a, in consecutive layers *)\nloopAt[ls_, i_] := Module[{a, b, j, side, chain},\n   If[! MatchQ[ls[[i]], {_, B[Subscript[\"coev\" | OverTilde[\"coev\"], _], {}, {_, _}]}], Return[$Failed]];\n   {a, b} = ls[[i]]; side = If[MatchQ[b, B[Subscript[OverTilde[\"coev\"], _], __]], a + 1, a];   (* left loop: chain on the right leg *)\n   j = i + 1; chain = {};\n   While[j <= Length[ls] && MatchQ[ls[[j]], {side, B[_, {_}, {_}]}] && ! MatchQ[ls[[j, 2, 1]], Subscript[\"coev\" | OverTilde[\"coev\"] | \"ev\" | OverTilde[\"ev\"], _]],\n    AppendTo[chain, ls[[j, 2]]]; j++];\n   If[j <= Length[ls] && MatchQ[ls[[j]], {a, B[Subscript[If[side == a + 1, \"ev\", OverTilde[\"ev\"]], _], {_, _}, {}]}],\n    {i, j, a, If[side == a + 1, \"left\", \"right\"], chain}, $Failed]];\nloopLayers[a_, \"left\", chain_] := With[{x = First[ins[First[chain]]]},\n   Join[{{a, B[coevR[x], {}, {star[x], x}]}}, {a + 1, #} & /@ chain, {{a, B[evL[x], {star[x], x}, {}]}}]];\nloopLayers[a_, \"right\", chain_] := With[{x = First[ins[First[chain]]]},\n   Join[{{a, B[coevL[x], {}, {x, star[x]}]}}, {a, #} & /@ chain, {{a, B[evR[x], {x, star[x]}, {}]}}]];\n(* the order of rotations: box names joined by \"|\" and compared code point by code point, as the editor does *)\nnameStr[s_String] := s; nameStr[s_] := ToString[s, InputForm];\nchainKey[ch_] := StringRiffle[nameStr /@ (sym /@ ch), \"|\"];\ncpLess[k1_String, k2_String] := Module[{x = ToCharacterCode[k1, \"Unicode\"], y = ToCharacterCode[k2, \"Unicode\"], i = 1},\n   While[i <= Min[Length[x], Length[y]] && x[[i]] == y[[i]], i++];\n   If[i > Min[Length[x], Length[y]], Length[x] < Length[y], x[[i]] < y[[i]]]];\nminRotation[ch_List] := Fold[If[cpLess[chainKey[#2], chainKey[#1]], #2, #1] &, ch, Table[RotateLeft[ch, r], {r, 1, Length[ch] - 1}]];\ntraceTurn[LD[src_, ls_]] := Catch[Do[With[{lp = loopAt[ls, i]},\n     If[lp =!= $Failed && Length[lp[[5]]] > 1,\n      With[{best = minRotation[lp[[5]]]},\n       If[best =!= lp[[5]], Throw[LD[src, Join[Take[ls, lp[[1]] - 1], loopLayers[lp[[3]], lp[[4]], best], Drop[ls, lp[[2]]]]]]]]]],\n    {i, Length[ls]}]; $Failed];\nsphericity[LD[src_, ls_]] := Catch[Do[With[{lp = loopAt[ls, i]},\n     If[lp =!= $Failed && lp[[4]] === \"right\",\n      Throw[LD[src, Join[Take[ls, lp[[1]] - 1],\n         If[lp[[5]] === {}, With[{x = unstar[ins[ls[[lp[[2]], 2]]][[2]]]}, {{lp[[3]], B[coevR[x], {}, {star[x], x}]}, {lp[[3]], B[evL[x], {star[x], x}, {}]}}],\n          loopLayers[lp[[3]], \"left\", lp[[5]]]], Drop[ls, lp[[2]]]]]]]], {i, Length[ls]}]; $Failed];\n(* loopAt needs a chain to name the colour of an empty right loop; handle it here *)\nsphericity0[LD[src_, ls_]] := Catch[Do[If[k < Length[ls] &&\n      MatchQ[ls[[k]], {a_, B[Subscript[\"coev\", x_], {}, {x_, _}]}] && MatchQ[ls[[k + 1]], {ls[[k, 1]], B[Subscript[OverTilde[\"ev\"], ls[[k, 2, 1, 2]]], _, {}]}],\n     With[{a = ls[[k, 1]], x = ls[[k, 2, 1, 2]]},\n      Throw[LD[src, Join[Take[ls, k - 1], {{a, B[coevR[x], {}, {star[x], x}]}, {a, B[evL[x], {star[x], x}, {}]}}, Drop[ls, k + 1]]]]]], {k, Length[ls]}]; $Failed];\nsphericityAll[ld_LD] := With[{r = sphericity0[ld]}, If[r =!= $Failed, r, sphericity[ld]]];\n\n(* whole-diagram rules: rewriteOnce gains the kind \"ld\" *)\nrewriteOnce[ld_LD, rs_Association] := Catch[\n   KeyValueMap[Function[{name, spec}, Switch[spec[[1]],\n      \"colour\", With[{new = recolour[ld, spec[[2]]]}, If[new =!= ld, Throw[{name, new}]]],\n      1, try1[ld, name, spec[[2]]],\n      2, try2[ld, name, spec[[2]]],\n      3, try3[ld, name, spec[[2]]],\n      \"ld\", With[{new = spec[[2]][ld]}, If[new =!= $Failed, Throw[{name, new}]]]]], rs];\n   $Failed];", "Input"],
Cell["44. The rule sets rulesD (pivotal) and rulesS (spherical)", "Section"],
Cell["rulesD = Join[rulesT, <|\n    \"Lemma 2.3 (X** = X)\" -> {1, lemma23strict},\n    \"\\[Psi] = id (X** = X)\" -> {1, psiStrict},\n    \"trace symmetry (\\[Section]2.6.1)\" -> {\"ld\", traceTurn},\n    \"inverse boxes\" -> {2, cancelInv},\n    \"naturality of \\[Psi] (\\[Section]2.5.1)\" -> {2, natPsi},\n    \"Lemma 2.3\" -> {1, lemma23}|>];\nrulesD[\"caps and cups on \\[CircleTimes]\"] = {1, nestCapsD};\nrulesS = Join[rulesD, <|\"sphericity (\\[Section]2.7.1)\" -> {\"ld\", sphericityAll}|>];", "Input"],
Cell["45. A matrix model: the pivotal category of weighted vector spaces (Example 2.7.2)", "Section"],
Cell["Each colour X is k^n with a weight w(X) \:2260 0; w(X* ) = 1/w(X), and weights multiply over \:2297. ev and coev are the usual pairing with the dual basis; \:1ebdv_X is w(X) times it and c\:0303oev_X is 1/w(X) times it, so all four duality identities hold. A box must keep the weight (w(source) = w(target)); then f* = f\:1d40 by either expression of Figure 2.3, so the category is pivotal. In it \:03c8_X = w(X)\:00b7id, dim_l(X) = n/w(X) and dim_r(X) = n\:00b7w(X). It is spherical exactly when every weight is \:00b11: this is Example 2.7.2 with d = w, made into vector spaces.\n   matW[ld, n, w, mats] multiplies the layers directly: n and w are functions of a base colour, mats gives the matrices of named boxes.", "Text"],
Cell["baseOf[c_String] := StringReplace[c, {\"*\" -> \"\", \"(\" -> \"\", \")\" -> \"\"}];\nstarDepth[c_String] := StringCount[c, \"*\"];\nwOf[c_String, w_] := Which[\n   StringStartsQ[c, \"(\"], 1/wOf[StringTake[c, {2, -3}], w],\n   StringContainsQ[c, \"\\[CircleTimes]\"], Times @@ (wOf[#, w] & /@ StringSplit[c, \"\\[CircleTimes]\"]),\n   starQ[c], 1/wOf[unstar[c], w], True, w[c]];\nnOf[c_String, n_] := Which[StringContainsQ[c, \"\\[CircleTimes]\"], Times @@ (nOf[#, n] & /@ StringSplit[baseOf[c], \"\\[CircleTimes]\"]), True, n[baseOf[c]]];\npairVec[k_] := Flatten[IdentityMatrix[k]];\nmatBox[b_B, n_, w_, mats_] := Module[{s = sym[b], i = ins[b], o = outs[b], c},\n   Which[\n    MatchQ[s, Subscript[\"id\", _]], IdentityMatrix[Times @@ (nOf[#, n] & /@ i)],\n    MatchQ[s, Subscript[\"ev\" | OverTilde[\"ev\"] | \"coev\" | OverTilde[\"coev\"], _]] && StringContainsQ[s[[2]], \"\\[CircleTimes]\"],\n     matW[LD[i, nestCaps[{0, b}]], n, w, mats],                                                  (* a nest of caps or cups *)\n    MatchQ[s, Subscript[\"ev\", _]], {pairVec[nOf[s[[2]], n]]},\n    MatchQ[s, Subscript[OverTilde[\"ev\"], _]], wOf[s[[2]], w] {pairVec[nOf[s[[2]], n]]},\n    MatchQ[s, Subscript[\"coev\", _]], Transpose[{pairVec[nOf[s[[2]], n]]}],\n    MatchQ[s, Subscript[OverTilde[\"coev\"], _]], Transpose[{pairVec[nOf[s[[2]], n]]}]/wOf[s[[2]], w],\n    MatchQ[s, Subscript[\"\\[Psi]\", _]], wOf[s[[2]], w] IdentityMatrix[nOf[s[[2]], n]],\n    MatchQ[s, Subscript[Superscript[\"\\[Psi]\", \"-1\"], _]], IdentityMatrix[nOf[s[[2]], n]]/wOf[s[[2]], w],\n    StringQ[s] && KeyExistsQ[mats, s], mats[s],\n    StringQ[s] && StringEndsQ[s, \"*\"], Transpose[matBox[B[StringDrop[s, -1], o, i], n, w, mats]],\n    True, mats[s]]];\nmatW[ld_LD, n_, w_, mats_] := Module[{rs = rows[ld], m},\n   m = IdentityMatrix[Times @@ (nOf[#, n] & /@ First[rs])];\n   Do[With[{a = ld[[2, k, 1]], b = ld[[2, k, 2]], row = rs[[k]]},\n     m = KroneckerProduct[IdentityMatrix[Times @@ (nOf[#, n] & /@ Take[row, a])], matBox[b, n, w, mats],\n         IdentityMatrix[Times @@ (nOf[#, n] & /@ Drop[row, a + Length[ins[b]]])]] . m], {k, Length[ld[[2]]]}];\n   m];", "Input"],
Cell["46. The constructions of pp. 38\:201350, as layered diagrams", "Section"],
Cell["SeedRandom[2026];\nnW = (2 &); wW = <|\"X\" -> 2, \"Y\" -> 2, \"Z\" -> 4, \"U\" -> 3, \"g\" -> 5|>;      (* weights: boxes X \:2192 Y and X\:2297Y \:2192 Z keep them *)\nmatsW = <|\"f\" -> RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {2, 2}], \"p\" -> RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {2, 2}], \"q\" -> RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {2, 2}],\n    \"h\" -> RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {2, 4}], \"k\" -> RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {2, 2}], \"u\" -> {{1, 1}, {0, 1}}, \"u\\[Prime]\" -> {{1, -1}, {0, 1}},\n    \"m\" -> RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {2, 2}], \"\\[Alpha]\" -> {{7}}|>;\nmW[ld_] := matW[ld, nW, wW, matsW];\ninverses = {{\"u\", \"u\\[Prime]\"}};      (* u\:2032 is declared the inverse of u *)\nfB = boxL[\"f\", {\"X\"}, {\"Y\"}];  pB = boxL[\"p\", {\"X\"}, {\"Y\"}];  qB = boxL[\"q\", {\"Y\"}, {\"X\"}];  kB2 = boxL[\"k\", {\"X\"}, {\"X\"}];\nhB2 = boxL[\"h\", {\"X\", \"Y\"}, {\"Z\"}];\n\n(* Lemma 2.2 *)\nlem22 = <|\"\\[Psi] = \\[Phi]\" -> {psiDef[\"X\"], phiDef[\"X\"]}, \"\\[Psi]\\:207b\\:00b9 = \\[CurlyTheta] = \\[Nu]\" -> {thetaDef[\"X\"], nuDef[\"X\"], boxL[psiInv[\"X\"], {\"X**\"}, {\"X\"}]},\n    \"\\[CurlyTheta]\\[Psi] = id\" -> {stackL[psiDef[\"X\"], thetaDef[\"X\"]], idL[{\"X\"}]}, \"\\[Psi]\\[CurlyTheta] = id\" -> {stackL[thetaDef[\"X\"], psiDef[\"X\"]], idL[{\"X**\"}]},\n    \"\\[Nu]\\[Phi] = id\" -> {stackL[phiDef[\"X\"], nuDef[\"X\"]], idL[{\"X\"}]}, \"\\[Phi]\\[Nu] = id\" -> {stackL[nuDef[\"X\"], phiDef[\"X\"]], idL[{\"X**\"}]}|>;\n(* Lemma 2.3: the four formulas, left side as typed in the book, right side the cap or cup on X* *)\nlem23 = <|\n   \"\\:1ebdv_X = ev_X* (\\[Psi]_X \\[CircleTimes] id_X* )\" -> {LD[{\"X\", \"X*\"}, {{0, B[evR[\"X\"], {\"X\", \"X*\"}, {}]}}],\n      LD[{\"X\", \"X*\"}, {{0, psiB[\"X\"]}, {0, B[evL[\"X*\"], {\"X**\", \"X*\"}, {}]}}]},\n   \"c\\:0303oev_X = (id_X* \\[CircleTimes] \\[Psi]\\:207b\\:00b9_X) coev_X*\" -> {LD[{}, {{0, B[coevR[\"X\"], {}, {\"X*\", \"X\"}]}}],\n      LD[{}, {{0, B[coevL[\"X*\"], {}, {\"X*\", \"X**\"}]}, {1, psiInvB[\"X\"]}}]},\n   \"ev_X = \\:1ebdv_X* (id_X* \\[CircleTimes] \\[Psi]_X)\" -> {LD[{\"X*\", \"X\"}, {{0, B[evL[\"X\"], {\"X*\", \"X\"}, {}]}}],\n      LD[{\"X*\", \"X\"}, {{1, psiB[\"X\"]}, {0, B[evR[\"X*\"], {\"X*\", \"X**\"}, {}]}}]},\n   \"coev_X = (\\[Psi]\\:207b\\:00b9_X \\[CircleTimes] id_X* ) c\\:0303oev_X*\" -> {LD[{}, {{0, B[coevL[\"X\"], {}, {\"X\", \"X*\"}]}}],\n      LD[{}, {{0, B[coevR[\"X*\"], {}, {\"X**\", \"X*\"}]}, {0, psiInvB[\"X\"]}}]}|>;\n(* Lemma 2.4 for S = ((X,\:2212),(Y,+)) and for S = ((X,+),(Y,+),(Z,\:2212)) *)\nS1 = {{\"X\", \"-\"}, {\"Y\", \"+\"}};  S2 = {{\"X\", \"+\"}, {\"Y\", \"+\"}, {\"Z\", \"-\"}};\nlem24[s_] := <|\n   \"ev_X_S (\\[CapitalPsi]_S* \\[CircleTimes] id) = ev_S\" -> {stackL[besideL[PsiS[dualTuple[s]], idL[XS[s]]], evXS[s]], evS[s]},\n   \"\\:1ebdv_X_S* (id \\[CircleTimes] \\[CapitalPsi]_S) = ev_S\" -> {stackL[besideL[idL[XS[dualTuple[s]]], PsiS[s]], evRXS[dualTuple[s]]], evS[s]},\n   \"(id \\[CircleTimes] \\[CapitalPsi]\\:207b\\:00b9_S* ) coev_X_S = coev_S\" -> {stackL[coevXS[s], besideL[idL[XS[s]], PsiInvS[dualTuple[s]]]], coevS[s]},\n   \"(\\[CapitalPsi]\\:207b\\:00b9_S \\[CircleTimes] id) c\\:0303oev_X_S* = coev_S\" -> {stackL[coevRXS[dualTuple[s]], besideL[PsiInvS[s], idL[XS[dualTuple[s]]]]], coevS[s]}|>;\n(* Exercise 2.3.3: \:03c8_X* = (\:03c8_X\:207b\:00b9)* , and (\:03c8_X)* \:03c8_X* = id *)\nex233 = <|\"\\[Psi]_X* = (\\[Psi]\\:207b\\:00b9_X)*\" -> {LD[{\"X*\"}, {{0, psiB[\"X*\"]}}], dualLD[LD[{\"X**\"}, {{0, psiInvB[\"X\"]}}]]},\n    \"(\\[Psi]_X)* \\[Psi]_X* = id_X*\" -> {stackL[LD[{\"X*\"}, {{0, psiB[\"X*\"]}}], dualLD[LD[{\"X\"}, {{0, psiB[\"X\"]}}]]], idL[{\"X*\"}]}|>;\n(* (2.3) and (2.4) *)\nzig23[s_] := {stackL[besideL[coevS[s], idL[XS[s]]], besideL[idL[XS[s]], evS[s]]], idL[XS[s]]};\nzig24[s_] := {stackL[besideL[idL[XS[dualTuple[s]]], coevS[s]], besideL[evS[s], idL[XS[dualTuple[s]]]]], idL[XS[dualTuple[s]]]};\n(* Lemma 2.5 / naturality of \:03c8: a box turned through 360\:00b0 *)\nrot = <|\"f turned through 360\\[Degree]\" -> {rotate360[fB], fB}, \"h : X\\[CircleTimes]Y \\[RightArrow] Z turned through 360\\[Degree]\" -> {rotate360[hB2], hB2}|>;\n(* \:00a72.6 traces *)\ntrc = <|\n   \"tr_l(pq) = tr_l(qp)\" -> {trL[stackL[qB, pB]], trL[stackL[pB, qB]]},\n   \"tr_r(pq) = tr_r(qp)\" -> {trR[stackL[qB, pB]], trR[stackL[pB, qB]]},\n   \"tr_l(f) = tr_r(f* )\" -> {trL[kB2], trR[boxL[\"k*\", {\"X*\"}, {\"X*\"}]]},\n   \"tr_r(f) = tr_l(f* )\" -> {trR[kB2], trL[boxL[\"k*\", {\"X*\"}, {\"X*\"}]]},\n   \"tr_l(f) = tr_l(f** )\" -> {trL[kB2], trL[dualLD[dualLD[kB2]]]},\n   \"tr_l(f \\[CircleTimes] g) = tr_l(tr_l(f)\\[CenterDot]g)\" -> {trL[LD[{\"X\", \"Y\"}, {{0, B[\"k\", {\"X\"}, {\"X\"}]}, {1, B[\"m\", {\"Y\"}, {\"Y\"}]}}]],\n      stackL[LD[{}, {{0, B[coevR[\"Y\"], {}, {\"Y*\", \"Y\"}]}}], besideL[idL[{\"Y*\"}], trL[kB2], boxL[\"m\", {\"Y\"}, {\"Y\"}]], LD[{\"Y*\", \"Y\"}, {{0, B[evL[\"Y\"], {\"Y*\", \"Y\"}, {}]}}]]},\n   \"tr_l(f\\[CenterDot]\\[Alpha]) = \\[Alpha] tr_l(f)\" -> {trL[besideL[kB2, boxL[\"\\[Alpha]\", {}, {}]]], stackL[trL[kB2], boxL[\"\\[Alpha]\", {}, {}]]},\n   \"tr_l on X*: ev_X* (id \\[CircleTimes] f) c\\:0303oev_X* = \\:1ebdv_X (id \\[CircleTimes] f) coev_X\" -> {trL[boxL[\"k*\", {\"X*\"}, {\"X*\"}]],\n      LD[{}, {{0, B[coevL[\"X\"], {}, {\"X\", \"X*\"}]}, {1, B[\"k*\", {\"X*\"}, {\"X*\"}]}, {0, B[evR[\"X\"], {\"X\", \"X*\"}, {}]}}]},\n   \"tr_r on X*: \\:1ebdv_X* (f \\[CircleTimes] id) coev_X* = ev_X (f \\[CircleTimes] id) c\\:0303oev_X\" -> {trR[boxL[\"k*\", {\"X*\"}, {\"X*\"}]],\n      LD[{}, {{0, B[coevR[\"X\"], {}, {\"X*\", \"X\"}]}, {0, B[\"k*\", {\"X*\"}, {\"X*\"}]}, {0, B[evL[\"X\"], {\"X*\", \"X\"}, {}]}}]}|>;\ndms = <|\"dim_l(X) = dim_r(X* )\" -> {dimL[\"X\"], dimR[\"X*\"]}, \"dim_l(X) = dim_l(X** )\" -> {dimL[\"X\"], dimL[\"X**\"]},\n    \"dim_r(X) = dim_l(X* )\" -> {dimR[\"X\"], dimL[\"X*\"]}, \"dim_r(X) = dim_r(X** )\" -> {dimR[\"X\"], dimR[\"X**\"]},\n    \"isomorphic objects: tr_l(u\\[Prime]u) = tr_l(uu\\[Prime])\" -> {trL[stackL[boxL[\"u\", {\"X\"}, {\"Y\"}], boxL[\"u\\[Prime]\", {\"Y\"}, {\"X\"}]]],\n      trL[stackL[boxL[\"u\\[Prime]\", {\"Y\"}, {\"X\"}], boxL[\"u\", {\"X\"}, {\"Y\"}]]]}|>;\n(* Exercise 2.4.4: a loop reversed and recoloured X* *)\nex244 = <|\"loop reversed: ev_X c\\:0303oev_X = \\:1ebdv_X* coev_X*\" -> {dimL[\"X\"], dimR[\"X*\"]},\n    \"loop with a box, reversed: tr_l(f) = tr_r(f* )\" -> {trL[kB2], trR[boxL[\"k*\", {\"X*\"}, {\"X*\"}]]}|>;\n(* Theorem 2.7, strand by strand: \:03c8_(X\:2297Y) is \:03c8_X \:2297 \:03c8_Y *)\npsiXY = LD[{\"X\", \"Y\"}, {{2, B[coevL[\"Y*\\[CircleTimes]X*\"], {}, {\"Y*\", \"X*\", \"X**\", \"Y**\"}]}, {0, B[evR[\"X\\[CircleTimes]Y\"], {\"X\", \"Y\", \"Y*\", \"X*\"}, {}]}}];\nthm27 = <|\"\\[Psi]_(X\\[CircleTimes]Y) = \\[Psi]_X \\[CircleTimes] \\[Psi]_Y\" -> {psiXY, besideL[LD[{\"X\"}, {{0, psiB[\"X\"]}}], LD[{\"Y\"}, {{0, psiB[\"Y\"]}}]]}|>;\n(* \:00a72.7 sphericity *)\nsph = <|\"tr_l(f) = tr_r(f)\" -> {trL[kB2], trR[kB2]}, \"dim_l(X) = dim_r(X)\" -> {dimL[\"X\"], dimR[\"X\"]},\n    \"Lemma 2.9: tr_r(pq) = tr_l(qp), a loop pushed across \\[Infinity]\" -> {trR[stackL[qB, pB]], trL[stackL[pB, qB]]}|>;", "Input"],
Cell["47. Checking an identity by the rules and in the matrix model", "Section"],
Cell["byRules[{l__}, rs_: rulesD] := SameQ @@ (simplifyLD[#, rs] & /@ {l});\ninMatrices[{l__}, w_: wW] := Equal @@ (matW[#, nW, w, matsW] & /@ {l});\nstepsKeepW[ld_, rs_: rulesD, w_: wW] := Equal @@ (matW[#[[2]], nW, w, matsW] & /@ simplifyTrace[ld, rs]);", "Input"],
Cell["47a. Walkthrough: the constructions step by step", "Section"],
Cell["These pictures come after the rule sets, which they use.", "Text"],
Cell["\:00a72.3.1 \:03c8_X and Lemma 2.2", "Subsection"],
Cell["\:03c8_X written out reduces to the box \:03c8_X: Lemma 2.3 turns the cup coev_X* into c\:0303oev_X with \:03c8_X on the X** leg, and the right zigzag straightens the rest.", "Text"],
Cell["showTraceP[simplifyTrace[psiDef[\"X\"], rulesD]]", "Input"],
Cell["Lemma 2.2: \:03d1_X \:03c8_X = id_X. Both \:03c8_X and \:03d1_X are written out; the rules leave nothing.", "Text"],
Cell["showTraceP[simplifyTrace[stackL[psiDef[\"X\"], thetaDef[\"X\"]], rulesD]]", "Input"],
Cell["\:00a72.3.2 ev_S and Lemma 2.4", "Subsection"],
Cell["The book's example for n = 2: ev_((X,\:2212),(Y,+)) : (Y* \:2297 X) \:2297 (X* \:2297 Y) \:2192 \|01d7d9, a cap \:1ebdv_X inside a cap ev_Y.", "Text"],
Cell["showP[evS[{{\"X\", \"-\"}, {\"Y\", \"+\"}}]]", "Input"],
Cell["Lemma 2.4 for S = ((X,\:2212),(Y,+)): ev_X_S (\:03a8_S* \:2297 id_X_S) reduces to ev_S.", "Text"],
Cell["showTraceP[simplifyTrace[lem24[S1][[1, 1]], rulesD]]", "Input"],
Cell["\:00a72.4 a box turned through 360\:00b0", "Subsection"],
Cell["The box f : X \:2192 Y turned through 360\:00b0 (the left picture of p. 43, with the \:03c8's of \:00a72.5.1 at the ends). Two folds give f**, naturality of \:03c8 gives \:03c8_Y f, and \:03c8_Y\:207b\:00b9 \:03c8_Y cancels.", "Text"],
Cell["showTraceP[simplifyTrace[rotate360[fB], rulesD]]", "Input"],
Cell["A box with two inputs, h : X \:2297 Y \:2192 Z, turned through 360\:00b0. The rules fold only boxes with one input and one output, so they stop part way; the matrices confirm that the picture is h (section 48).", "Text"],
Cell["showP[simplifyLD[rotate360[hB2], rulesD]]", "Input"],
Cell["\:00a72.6 traces and dimensions", "Subsection"],
Cell["tr_l(pq) and tr_l(qp): the loop is turned so that its boxes start at p in both.", "Text"],
Cell["Column[{showTraceP[simplifyTrace[trL[stackL[qB, pB]], rulesD]], showP[simplifyLD[trL[stackL[pB, qB]], rulesD]]}, Spacings -> 2]", "Input"],
Cell["dim_l(X**) reduces to dim_l(X): Lemma 2.3 twice on each of the cap and the cup, and the \:03c8's cancel.", "Text"],
Cell["showTraceP[simplifyTrace[dimL[\"X**\"], rulesD]]", "Input"],
Cell["the rule sets", "Subsection"],
Cell["Keys[rulesS]", "Input"],
Cell["the matrix model", "Subsection"],
Cell["In the model with weights w(X) = w(Y) = 2: \:03c8_X = 2\:00b7id, dim_l(X) = 1 and dim_r(X) = 4, so this pivotal category is not spherical. With weights \:00b11 it is.", "Text"],
Cell["{mW[LD[{\"X\"}, {{0, psiB[\"X\"]}}]], mW[dimL[\"X\"]], mW[dimR[\"X\"]], matW[dimL[\"X\"], nW, <|\"X\" -> -1|>, matsW], matW[dimR[\"X\"], nW, <|\"X\" -> -1|>, matsW]}", "Input"],
Cell["the lists of identities", "Subsection"],
Cell["Each entry is a list of diagrams that should represent one morphism; the first is usually the left side as the book writes it.", "Text"],
Cell["Length /@ {lem22, lem23, lem24[S1], ex233, rot, trc, dms, ex244, thm27, sph}", "Input"],
Cell["48. Tests", "Section"],
Cell["Each identity of pp. 38\:201350 is checked three ways: the rules bring all its sides to one normal form, the sides have the same matrix in the weighted model of section 45 (w(X) = w(Y) = 2, so \:03c8_X = 2\:00b7id and the category is not spherical), and no step of the simplification changes the matrix. The \:00a72.7 identities hold only in a spherical category: they fail in this model and with rulesD, and hold with weights \:00b11 and with rulesS.", "Text"],
Cell["all48 = Join[lem22, lem23, KeyMap[\"S1: \" <> # &, lem24[S1]], KeyMap[\"S2: \" <> # &, lem24[S2]], ex233,\n   <|\"(2.3) S1\" -> zig23[S1], \"(2.3) S2\" -> zig23[S2], \"(2.4) S1\" -> zig24[S1], \"(2.4) S2\" -> zig24[S2]|>,\n   KeyDrop[rot, {\"h : X\\[CircleTimes]Y \\[RightArrow] Z turned through 360\\[Degree]\"}], trc, dms, ex244, thm27];\nspherical = <|\"X\" -> -1, \"Y\" -> -1, \"Z\" -> 1, \"U\" -> 1, \"g\" -> 1|>;\n<|\n \"by the rules (rulesD)\" -> AllTrue[Values[all48], byRules],\n \"in the weighted model (w(X) = 2)\" -> AllTrue[Values[all48], inMatrices],\n \"every step keeps the matrix\" -> AllTrue[Flatten[Values[all48], 1], stepsKeepW],\n \"h turned through 360\\[Degree], in matrices\" -> inMatrices[rot[\"h : X\\[CircleTimes]Y \\[RightArrow] Z turned through 360\\[Degree]\"]],\n \"not spherical: tr_l(f) \\[NotEqual] tr_r(f) when w(X) = 2\" -> (! inMatrices[sph[\"tr_l(f) = tr_r(f)\"]]),\n \"not spherical: the rules of rulesD keep tr_l(f) and tr_r(f) apart\" -> (! byRules[sph[\"tr_l(f) = tr_r(f)\"]]),\n \"spherical (w = \\[PlusMinus]1): \:00a72.7 identities in matrices\" -> AllTrue[Values[sph], inMatrices[#, spherical] &],\n \"spherical: \:00a72.7 identities by rulesS\" -> AllTrue[Values[sph], byRules[#, rulesS] &],\n \"Example 2.7.2: dim_l = 1/d, dim_r = d\" -> (matW[dimL[\"g\"], (1 &), <|\"g\" -> 5|>, matsW] == {{1/5}} && matW[dimR[\"g\"], (1 &), <|\"g\" -> 5|>, matsW] == {{5}}),\n \"strict inputs (X** = X): \:03c8_X written out is id_X\" ->\n   (simplifyLD[LD[{\"X\"}, {{1, B[coevL[\"X*\"], {}, {\"X*\", \"X\"}]}, {0, B[evR[\"X\"], {\"X\", \"X*\"}, {}]}}], rulesD] === idL[{\"X\"}]),\n \"\:00a72.1\:20132.2 results unchanged under rulesD\" -> (simplifyLD[fsL, rulesD] === fstarL && And @@ (sameQ[#[[1]], #[[2]], rulesD] & /@ fig24) &&\n     simplifyLD[ex225a, rulesD] === idL[{\"X*\", \"Y*\"}] && sameQ[fig25LD, penroseLD[fig25src, fig25flat], rulesD])\n|>", "Input"],
Cell["Appendix: what is and is not mechanised", "Section"],
Cell["Double duals are honest objects: X** is not identified with X. Lemma 2.3 is a rewrite rule that trades a cap or cup coloured X* for one coloured X and a box \:03c8^{\:00b11}_X; with \"inverse boxes\" and \"naturality of \:03c8\" it proves Lemma 2.2, Lemma 2.3, Lemma 2.4 (for the tuples S1, S2), Exercise 2.3.3, Theorem 2.7 strand by strand, dim_l(X) = dim_l(X**), tr_l(f) = tr_l(f**) and a one-line box turned through 360\:00b0.", "Item"],
Cell["The editor identifies X** with X and \:03c8_X with id_X (a strict pivotal category). For such inputs the kernel uses the strict forms of the rules, \"Lemma 2.3 (X** = X)\" and \"\:03c8 = id (X** = X)\", so both engines agree.", "Item"],
Cell["Theorem 2.7 is checked with the monoidal constraints of the dual functor written as identities, which is how the tensor rules of section 30 read (X \:2297 Y)*. Its full proof on p. 46 needs those constraints as boxes; that is not mechanised.", "Item"],
Cell["Lemma 2.5 is checked for boxes with one input and one output by the rules, and for h : X \:2297 Y \:2192 Z in matrices only: the folds of Figure 2.3 are implemented for one-line boxes.", "Item"],
Cell["Trace symmetry is a whole-diagram rule: a loop whose boxes sit on one leg, in consecutive layers, is turned to a fixed starting box. It does not reach loops with boxes on both legs or other boxes interleaved.", "Item"],
Cell["Not mechanised: \:00a72.4.3's replacement of a rectangle by a box (it is the definition of composition), pure categories and \:2297-multiplicativity of traces (checked in matrices only), Lemma 2.8 and Exercise 2.5.2 on pivotal functors, Exercise 2.4.4 for a recoloured loop (only the reversed loop is checked), and \:00a72.7.3.", "Item"],
Cell["\:00a9 Computational Classnotes \:00b7 CC BY-NC-SA 4.0", "Text"]
}, StyleDefinitions -> "Default.nb"]
